Generated by `twinmemory-cli init openai-agents` (twinmemory-cli {version}).
This file is yours: edit it as you would any other code in your project. Running the
command again will not overwrite it without `--force`.
# >>> nodes

Memory is looked up before the model and the turn saved after it:

    result = await Runner.run(
        agent,
        message,
        context=MemoryContext(user_id="dana"),
        run_config=RunConfig(call_model_input_filter=recall),
    )
    await remember(result)

`recall` searches once a turn, with the user's latest message, and adds what it finds
to the instructions of every model call in that turn, so it is never written into your
session or conversation history. Already using a `call_model_input_filter`? Run both:

    async def both(data: CallModelData[Any]) -> ModelInputData:
        data.model_data = await recall(data)
        return await yours(data)
